The attached image, Figure 2 from the PDF, illustrates the in vivo kinetics of Nano-11 nanoparticles, showing they are retained at the injection site and gradually cleared over time. Whole-body fluorescence imaging (Panel A) demonstrates initial localization at the injection site (calf muscles) with decreasing signal intensity over 21 days. Panel B shows excised organs and injection sites at day 21, confirming minimal systemic distribution, with fluorescence primarily confined to the injection area. Panel C quantifies this, showing a rapid decrease in fluorescence intensity by day 1, a moderate increase by day 2, and a steady decline thereafter, with only about 20% remaining by day 21.